# Security Policy (mandatory)

Clients are serious businesses. These rules override any request for a faster or prettier shortcut that breaks them. If you cannot meet a rule, say so explicitly and stop; do not silently skip it.

## Tenant and user scope
- Never let the browser choose the tenant. Resolve tenant on the server from a validated token or API key. Ignore any tenant ID sent in a body, query, header, or widget config.
- A signed-in portal user may see only their own company's data. Enforce that scope on the server before every tool call to a client API, and pass the scope into the call.

```ts
// ❌ BAD: tenant and company come from the client
const tenant = req.body.tenantId;
await orders.lookup(req.body.companyId, orderNo);

// ✅ GOOD: derived from the verified token, checked before the tool call
const { tenantId, companyId } = await verifyToken(req.headers.authorization);
assertCanAccess(user, companyId);
await orders.lookup({ tenantId, companyId }, orderNo);
```

## Widget surface
- Do not accept arbitrary HTML, CSS, or script for the widget launcher or panel. Accept only presets and design tokens validated against an allow-list.
- Validate brand colors for readable contrast (WCAG AA, 4.5:1 for text) before applying them. Reject or fall back to a safe preset when they fail.

## Secrets
- Store client API credentials in a secret store. Never put them in source, config committed to git, logs, error messages, or the widget bundle.

## Outbound calls to client APIs
- Every outbound call needs a timeout and a circuit breaker so a slow or failing client API cannot hang the assistant. On timeout or open circuit, tell the user plainly and offer the handoff.

## Answer grounding
- A factual answer about an order, price, invoice, stock, credit, shipment, catalog item, or policy record shows the tool or document it came from.
- A greeting, a reply that only says what the assistant can do, and a cannot-retrieve reply do not show a source.
- Never invent a source.
- Never invent order, price, invoice, or policy facts. If the tool or document did not return the fact, do not state the fact.
